desc:GFX Lab Sidebar - the SIDEBAR peak saturation (include)
//author: JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// gfx-lab-sidebar - the WS9 series' SIDEBAR stage (JGWizrad's design, 30 Oct 2026; first in WS9 Channel). JG: "sidebar"
// is the concept's name, not "headroom".
// The signal is padded 18 dB inside the stage; only the peaks that still reach the stage's ceiling are saturated; what
// the saturation adds (the "sidebar") is lifted back 18 dB and folded into the clean, full-level signal. The clean
// signal is never squashed below the ceiling; the peaks gain harmonics.
//
// The curve: below the knee (a little lower on the positive side, for some 2nd harmonic) nothing happens; above it
// the excess goes through x / sqrt(1 + x^2) scaled to the knee, so the join is smooth (slope 1, no bend at the first
// point) and the curve tends to twice the knee. The sidebar = the curve minus the padded signal (zero below the knee),
// x 1 / pad, DC-blocked (5 Hz), high-passed by TONE (one pole) and smoothed (one-pole low-pass, 15 kHz). It comes out
// on the same sample as the input: add it to that sample and the two stay in time and in phase.
// Run it inside the unit's oversampled section (gfx-lab-os) - it makes harmonics.
//
// API (all rates are the RUNNING rate, srate x os_f)
//   sb_rate(fs)                         @init, on a sample-rate change and on os_chg: the rate's coefficients
//   sb_target(hr_db, amt, on, tone, hb) @block: the ceiling in dB above 0 VU (-18 dBFS; 6 - 24 typical), the amount
//                                       (1 = what a stage with that headroom would add = plain saturation at the
//                                       ceiling, 2 = twice that), on (0 / 1), TONE in Hz (22 - 2200), hb = supply
//                                       headroom factor (1 = nominal; > 1 = a sagging supply, the knee comes down)
//   sb_snap()                           after the first sb_target: no glide in
//   sb_glide(kk, ks)                    @sample (base rate): glides the knee (kk, ~30 ms) and the amount / on (ks, ~15 ms)
//   sb_ctl(k)                           every 32 base samples: glides TONE and works its coefficient
//   u.sb_run(x)                         one running-rate sample in -> the sidebar to add (already x the amount);
//                                       sb_pk holds the largest |sidebar| since the unit last cleared it (for a meter)
//   u.sb_clr()                          clear the state (after a factor change, after REAPER's bypass)
// Variables: sb_ (this file's prefix).

@init
SB_PAD = 0.12589254117941673; SB_RST = 1 / SB_PAD;      // -18 dB in, +18 dB back
function sb_sat(x) ( x / sqrt(1 + x * x); );
function sb_rate(fs) local(w) (
  sb_fs = fs; w = 2 * $pi / fs;
  sb_dcc = 1 - 5 * w; sb_lpk = 1 - exp(-15000 * w); sb_ha = exp(-exp(sb_fz) * w);
);
function sb_target(hr_db, amt, on, tone, hb) (
  sb_tt = exp((-36 + hr_db) * 0.11512925464970228) / max(hb, 0.1);   // the knee in the padded signal (0 VU = -36 dBFS there)
  sb_gt = max(amt, 0) * (on >= 0.5);
  sb_fzt = log(min(max(tone, 22), 2200));
);
function sb_snap() ( sb_t = sb_tt; sb_g = sb_gt; sb_fz = sb_fzt; sb_ha = exp(-2 * $pi * exp(sb_fz) / sb_fs); );
function sb_glide(kk, ks) ( sb_t += (sb_tt - sb_t) * kk; sb_g += (sb_gt - sb_g) * ks; sb_tp = sb_t * 0.88; sb_tn = sb_t * 1.12; );
function sb_ctl(k) ( sb_fz += (sb_fzt - sb_fz) * k; sb_ha = exp(-2 * $pi * exp(sb_fz) / sb_fs); );
function sb_run(x) instance(dx, dy, hx, hy, lp) local(p, a, t, d) (
  p = x * SB_PAD; a = abs(p);
  t = p >= 0 ? sb_tp : sb_tn;
  d = a > t ? ( (t + t * sb_sat((a - t) / t)) * (p >= 0 ? 1 : -1) - p ) : 0;
  d *= SB_RST;
  dy = d - dx + sb_dcc * dy; dx = d;
  hy = sb_ha * (hy + dy - hx); hx = dy;
  lp += (hy - lp) * sb_lpk;
  abs(lp) < 0.000000000001 ? lp = 0;
  d = lp * sb_g; sb_pk = max(sb_pk, abs(d));
  d;
);
function sb_clr() instance(dx, dy, hx, hy, lp) ( dx = dy = hx = hy = lp = 0; );
